# A table struct with a field type that has no SQL column mapping (a nested
# struct here) is rejected by Sema in ALL build modes with a located error —
# the row mapper would otherwise leave the field silently null (null-deref on
# first access at runtime).
^[^:]+\.b:[0-9]+:[0-9]+: error: table struct 'Customer' field 'address' has type 'Address', which has no SQL column mapping
